    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-16 (round 13).**\n\n**Symptom.** 425 edges (0.4% of 96,864 total) on hypergumbo's self-analysis have empty `origin_run_id`, plus 1 edge has BOTH `origin` and `origin_run_id` empty. Breakdown:\n\n| Count | origin | type | Notes |\n|---:|---|---|---|\n| 291 | `decorator-dispatch-linker-v1` | `dispatches_to` | Origin stamped, run_id missing |\n| 127 | `enclosure-linker-v1` | `uses` | Origin stamped, run_id missing |\n| 6 | `json-v1` | `depends_on` | Origin stamped, run_id missing |\n| **1** | `''` (empty) | `module_attr_ref` | **Both origin AND run_id empty** |\n\nThe lone edge with both empty is from `packages/htrac-frontend/src/sw-register.ts:16` → `navigator.serviceWorker` (browser global), produced by the JS module linker:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"edge:sha256:a13fbe67509f3b3b\",\n  \"edge_key\": \"edgekey:sha256:309b82c85d21e83c\",\n  \"src\": \"typescript:packages/htrac-frontend/src/sw-register.ts:1-24:<module:sw-register.ts>:module\",\n  \"dst\": \"typescript:navigator:0-0:navigator.serviceWorker:attribute\",\n  \"type\": \"module_attr_ref\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"origin\": \"\",\n  \"origin_run_id\": \"\",\n  \"origin_run_signature\": null,\n  \"meta\": {\"evidence_type\": \"module_attribute_reference\"}\n}\n```\n\n**Why this is a problem.**\n\n1. **Partial provenance.** 425 edges have `origin` (which linker produced them) but no `origin_run_id` (which specific analysis pass instance). For reproducibility/debugging, you can answer \"what linker created this?\" but not \"during which analysis run, with what config.\" \n\n2. **One edge with no provenance at all.** This single TypeScript edge has zero attribution. If a downstream tool flags it as a bug (\"why is `navigator.serviceWorker` in the call graph as a module_attr_ref?\"), there's no way to trace it back to the producer without grep-walking the codebase.\n\n3. **Edge-side analog of INV-sopon.** INV-sopon documented that 19 of 21 linkers fail to stamp Symbol.origin on synthesized Symbols. This finding extends that pattern to Edges:\n   - Symbol.origin gap → INV-sopon (filed round 2)\n   - Edge.origin + Edge.origin_run_id gap → this item\n\nSame underlying discipline failure: producers don't stamp provenance consistently.\n\n**Invariant statement.** Every Edge must have a non-empty `origin` field (declaring which producer emitted it) and a non-empty `origin_run_id` field (declaring which analysis-run instance produced it). The Edge dataclass should enforce this at construction time (similar to how Edge enforces `edge_key` and `id` fields).\n\n**Severity.** Low-medium. Small surface (0.4% of edges) but generalizes — any new linker that follows the existing patterns will inherit the gap. Adjacent to INV-sopon's broader Symbol-side issue.\n\n**Fix proposal.**\n\n1. **Enforce in Edge.__post_init__** (or factory). Raise if `origin` or `origin_run_id` is empty/None. Forces producers to plumb the values through.\n\n2. **Audit the 3 specific linkers** that produce most of the 425:\n   - `linkers/decorator_dispatch.py` (291 missing run_id)\n   - `linkers/enclosure.py` (127 missing run_id)\n   - `linkers/json.py` (6 missing run_id)\n   - js_module-linker's TypeScript module_attr_ref path (1 with both empty)\n\n3. **Backfill via the existing run-context plumbing.** Linkers receive a `LinkerContext` that should already have access to the run signature; the values just aren't being passed through to Edge construction.\n\n**Test gap.** Property test on the self-analysis fixture: assert every edge has `origin != \"\" and origin_run_id != \"\"`. Currently 425 violations.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py` — Edge dataclass (`origin`, `origin_run_id` fields)\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/decorator_dispatch.py` — 291 missing\n- `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/enclosure.py` — 127 missing\n- `INV-sopon-...` (filed round 2) — Symbol.origin gap across 19 linkers; this is the Edge-side sibling\n- `INV-mopif-...` (filed round 11) — HTTP linker creates Symbols with empty origin; related discipline issue"  # cdb3
    fields: {}  # cdb3
